{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\n- `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml:203` (origin/main 9f8b2af21c8) sets `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED: \"1\"` unconditionally on the `Run mutation shard` step of the `bounded mutation gate` job. Comments at `_mutation.yml:92-94`, `:187-189` and `:197-199` justify it with \"Hosted Ubuntu denies unprivileged CLONE_NEWUSER\".\n- Run 41939410124 (Gerrit change 3328, 2026-11-04 PST), job 126957533578, `Image: ubuntu-24.04`: the step env shows `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED: 1`, then `bwrap is installed but cannot create a namespace (bwrap: setting up uid map: Permission denied)` and `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED is set: running mutation tests UNSANDBOXED`. All 7 shards concluded `success`. The waiver appears only as a log warning; `summary.json` (built in `scripts/mutation_gate.py` `run_gate`, lines 698-745) has no sandbox field, so a waived pass and a sandboxed pass produce identical evidence and an identical Verified vote.\n- Run 42949111146 (2026-11-10 PST), job 130289932461, `Image: ubuntu-26.04`, `bubblewrap 0.11.1`: no namespace warning, no waiver line, `\"outcome\": \"success\"`. `ubuntu-latest` now resolves to 26.04 and bwrap works there since `aa9828f9a2b` (`unwasteful-increased-colt`, bind only outermost paths).\n\n## Root cause\nThe workflow pre-sets the operator waiver, so `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py` `wrap()` (lines 201-224) takes its `opt_out_enabled(env)` branch and returns argv unwrapped whenever `probe()` finds no working mechanism, instead of raising `SandboxUnavailable`. Separately, if `SandboxUnavailable` were raised, `mutation_gate.main()` (line 777) catches only `GateError`, so the shard would die with a traceback and write no `summary.json`.\n\n## Impact\nOn a runner where bwrap cannot create a namespace, mutated code runs with write access to the whole runner and the gate still reports green as though sandboxed. The 2026-08-26 destructive-mutation incident (`e668-b496-e264-4283`) is the hazard the sandbox exists for.\n\n## Approach\n1. `_mutation.yml`: delete the `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED` env line and rewrite the three stale comments to say bwrap starts on the hosted image and the lane fails closed without it. Rationale: the evidence above shows hosted 26.04 runs sandboxed, so the waiver no longer buys availability and only removes protection.\n2. `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py`: add `UNSANDBOXED = \"unsandboxed\"` and `mechanism(env) -> str`, which returns `probe()`'s result, or `UNSANDBOXED` when the operator waiver is set, or raises `SandboxUnavailable`. `wrap()` calls it, so wrapping behaviour is unchanged. The local operator waiver stays (documented in `docs/local-dev-env.md`); this adds no config key, env var or feature flag.\n3. `scripts/mutation_gate.py`: `RunResults` gains a `sandbox: str` field. `execute_shard` calls `mutation_sandbox.mechanism(env)` before running anything and converts `SandboxUnavailable` to `GateError(\"sandbox-unavailable\", ...)`, so `main()` writes `summary.json` with `failure_class: sandbox-unavailable` and the detail names the missing sandbox. Each shard summary records `\"sandbox\": {\"base\": <mechanism or null>, \"head\": <mechanism>}`.\n4. Docs: `docs/mutation-testing.md` and `docs/local-dev-env.md` state that CI sets no waiver and that `summary.json` records the mechanism.\n\n## Testing\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py`: `mechanism()` returns the probed mechanism, returns `unsandboxed` under the waiver, raises without it.\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py`: a `run`-path test with `probe` patched to `None` and no waiver asserts exit 1 and `summary.json` `failure_class == \"sandbox-unavailable\"` with the detail naming `bwrap`; existing `run_gate` tests assert the per-shard `sandbox` record; a workflow test asserts no step env in `_mutation.yml` sets `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED`.\n- `make verify` green; the Gerrit Verified run for the change touches `scripts/mutation_gate.py` (a global-support input in `.github/mutation-shards.toml`), so its mutation shards run without the waiver on hosted Ubuntu and must pass sandboxed.\n\n## Scope\n- `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml`\n- `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py`\n- `scripts/mutation_gate.py`\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py`\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py`\n- `docs/mutation-testing.md`, `docs/local-dev-env.md`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml` no longer sets `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED`, enforced by a test; with no working sandbox and no waiver, `mutation_gate.py run` exits 1 and writes `summary.json` with `failure_class` `sandbox-unavailable` and a detail naming the missing sandbox (asserted by a test).\n- [ ] `summary.json` records which sandbox mechanism ran each shard's base and head runs (asserted by a test), and the change's own CI mutation jobs show a non-`unsandboxed` mechanism in their published `summary.json` (run URL recorded on this ticket).\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the final patch set."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794371136206754499,"uuid":"facfeedd-750c-45bd-b367-fad4b8b88e96"}